 Team Reflections - Challenges & Lessons Learned
 Most Prominent Challenges
1. Data Extraction & Management
The Challenge:
Retrieving the required data from the source platform proved to be a significant challenge. Manual extraction was particularly difficult given that the dataset exceeded 3,000 medications.

Impact:

Time-consuming manual processes

Risk of data inconsistency

Difficulty maintaining accuracy with large datasets

Solution:

Automated data extraction scripts were developed

Batch processing was implemented

Data validation checks were added at each stage

2. Time Constraints & Learning Curve
The Challenge:
The timeframe was extremely tight for delivering a complete, error-free project. Additionally, Flutter was new to some team members, so the framework was being learned concurrently with application development — an approach that differed from the usual method of learning programming languages.

Impact:

Increased development time

Higher error rate during initial phases

Stress on team members

Solution:

Prioritized core MVP features

Allocated specific learning time

Used official documentation and tutorials

Leveraged community support (Stack Overflow, Flutter community)

3. Design Revisions & UI/UX Challenges
The Challenge:
Upon completing the application's UI design, it was rejected by the supervisor on both User Experience (UX) and User Interface (UI) grounds. The redesign process consumed considerable additional time and caused delays.

Impact:

Significant time delays

Demotivation among team members

Rework of completed components

Resolution:

After discussion, the decision was made to proceed with the original design

The original design better served the application's requirements

This experience highlighted the importance of clear design justification

Lesson Learned:

Always document design decisions with clear reasoning

Get early feedback before full implementation

Balance supervisor feedback with project requirements

4. Team Communication & Collaboration
The Challenge:
The team did not consistently keep all members informed of updates at the outset. When a personal circumstance prevented communication, this escalated into an issue.

Impact:

Misalignment on project status

Duplicate work

Frustration among team members

Resolution:

The issue was resolved through open discussion

Team members were able to clarify their perspectives

Improved communication protocols were established

Lesson Learned:

Regular check-ins are essential

Clear communication channels must be maintained

Personal circumstances should be communicated early

5. System Integration
The Challenge:
Connecting all the parts of the project together — the frontend, backend, and database — and making sure everything worked properly and cohesively. Issues arose during data exchange and integrating different features, especially with medication search and interaction checking.

Impact:

Integration delays

Data inconsistency issues

Feature malfunctions

Solution:

Continuous testing throughout development

Collaboration among team members

API testing with Postman before integration

Using proper error handling

6. Git & Version Control Conflicts
The Challenge:
Working with Git and resolving merge conflicts was challenging, especially when collaborating on shared files, with issues around branches, stashing changes, and pulling updates.

Impact:

Code loss

Integration delays

Frustration

Solution:

Learned Git branching basics

Practiced commands: git status, git stash, git pull, git merge

Improved workflow to avoid overlapping file edits

Resolved conflicts carefully by reviewing code changes

7. Understanding Project Structure
The Challenge:
The project had multiple directories (frontend, backend, migrations, etc.), and understanding where to place files and how to connect them was confusing at first.

Impact:

File placement errors

Import issues

Navigation difficulties

Solution:

Studied project structure thoroughly

Followed existing architecture patterns

Mastered separation of concerns:

views/ for UI

models/ for data structures

providers/ for state management

services/ for API calls

8. Testing the Code
The Challenge:
Writing meaningful tests for the Flutter code was difficult, with uncertainty about the difference between unit tests, widget tests, and integration tests.

Impact:

Low test coverage

Undetected bugs

Quality issues

Solution:

Researched Flutter testing best practices

Wrote unit tests for individual functions using flutter_test

Moved to widget tests for UI components

Used flutter test --coverage to track code coverage

9. Backend API Integration
The Challenge:
Connecting the Flutter frontend to the Node.js backend API was challenging, especially when dealing with authentication tokens (JWT), HTTP requests, and error responses from the server.

Impact:

Authentication failures

Data fetching issues

Poor user experience

Solution:

Used http package along with dio to send requests

Managed interceptors for token authentication

Tested API endpoints using Postman before integrating them into the app

Implemented proper error handling for API responses

 Most Important Lessons Learned
1. Workload Distribution
Lesson: Not to assume sole responsibility for large components of the project. Sharing tasks with the team enhances collaboration, reduces pressure on individual members, and ensures other team members do not underestimate the complexity of a component simply because they have not experienced it firsthand.

Application:

Distribute large features across multiple team members

Regular check-ins on progress

Pair programming for complex components

2. Collaboration Over Individual Work
Lesson: A project's success doesn't depend only on coding, but relies heavily on collaboration and communication among team members.

Key Takeaways:

Proper planning is essential

Clear task distribution prevents confusion

Continuous review helps catch issues early

Any modification in one part of the system can affect other parts

Result:

Better quality code

Fewer integration issues

Higher team morale

3. Contextual Decision-Making
Lesson: The experiences and mistakes of other teams do not necessarily predict identical outcomes for our own team. While external insights are valuable, they should not be allowed to unduly influence our team's decisions.

Application:

Consider team context when evaluating external advice

Adapt solutions to fit our specific project needs

Use external insights as reference, not as absolute rules

4. Self-Confidence & Vision
Lesson: The importance of maintaining self-confidence, even in discussions concerning a product that represents dedicated effort. Without this confidence, the original vision may become diluted, leading to numerous deviations and ultimately diminishing the passion and motivation required to complete the product.

Key Takeaways:

Trust your design decisions

Defend your work with reasoned arguments

Stay committed to the original vision while being open to feedback

5. Continuous Testing
Lesson: Ongoing testing helps detect issues early and saves time and effort.

Application:

Write tests alongside code

Run tests frequently during development

Use CI/CD for automated testing

Test API endpoints before frontend integration

6. Understanding the Tech Stack
Lesson: Learning a new framework while building an application is challenging but achievable with the right approach.

Strategies:

Start with official documentation

Watch tutorials for practical examples

Practice small components before integration

Rely on community support (Stack Overflow, forums)

Don't be afraid to ask for help

7. Time Management & Prioritization
Lesson: Managing a heavy workload and tight project deadlines requires effective prioritization.

Strategies:

Use a personal task list to prioritize work

Focus on completing core features first

Save minor UI or polish issues for later

Identify and address critical blockers early

